hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1335","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, narrated by al-Mu’tamir, who said: I heard Hisham, narrated by Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on the Day of the Battles: “What is the matter with them? God filled their graves and their houses with fire. They also distracted us from the middle prayer until \The sun went down\"""""""
"1336","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said The Day of the Trench: “May God fill their hearts and graves with fire as they distracted us from the middle prayer.”"
"1337","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Shutair ibn Shikal, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They have distracted us from the middle prayer.” The afternoon prayer, God filled their graves, or he said: Their houses with fire, and Al-Ashjaj said: Their houses and their graves with fire, then he prayed between the two evening prayers. Salam added: “Between Maghrib and Isha’”"
"1338","Ahmad ibn Mani` told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer.”"
